Provisional HTTPS-CLOSE-01 bounded repair review requirements

1. Register each request owner under a unique ID and capture publication generation before first send suspension.
2. At close entry, retire generation and clear only its channel/telemetry state before any await. Capture owners; cancel outside their locks and await independent non-consuming finish.
3. Retain retiring owners in the registry (or a closing group) until truly finished so duplicate close joins them too.
4. Request completion cleanup removes only its captured unique registry entry. Old close resumes without clearing new-generation state; old sender checks generation before path/peak/result publication.
5. Pre-start cancel+join must finish without requiring later read scheduling. A later read of that cancelled single-use object must throw the cancellation without creating a session; no post-close resurrection. Once startup is claimed, latch cancel and join through normal callback completion/invalidation.
6. Preflight deadline failure wakes all finish waiters and releases empty buffer; duplicate read does not clear another active invocation.
7. Started request join predicate must follow the delegate-queue tail acknowledgement, not merely invalidation callback entry. Separate waiters never consume sender Result.
8. Deterministic tests: real ready silent request close; duplicate close while held invalidation/finish; successful late response held before actor publication then closed; replacement request can publish while old cleanup resumes; pre-read cancellation/join then late read; expired deadline join.

No source/native changes by reviewer. Scope is HTTPS only. Existing detached TCP work is outside this repair; do not generalise HTTPS close proof to it.

